# Notes for users
notes: |
  This CFF file provides citation information for both the research paper and the software.
  
  **For citing the paper:**
  Use the preferred-citation entry; volume, issue and pages are filled in on acceptance.

  **For citing the software:**
  Use the top-level entry (title, version, DOI), which is what CFF describes by default.

  **For citing the dataset:**
  The StatsBomb Open Data is separately licensed under CC-BY-NC-4.0 and should be cited
  according to their requirements: https://github.com/statsbomb/open-data
  
  **For reproducibility:**
  All results can be reproduced from the committed artifacts in this repository.
  See README.md for complete reproduction instructions.
